/-!
# Polynomial data of the guiding-centre field (generated)

Polynomials in `(u, z, c, s)` (`u = R − 1`, `c = cos 2φ`, `s = sin 2φ`) used by the flow form of
the guiding-centre field `B̃ = B + ρ ∇×b` of the rational stellarator `B = field (1/4)`
(`Design/RationalStellaratorGCFlow`): the partial derivatives `∂_u, ∂_z, ∂_φ` of the field
polynomials `D, n_R, n_z` of `Design/KamNewtonField`, the Taylor polynomial `P(u)` of `R^{−3}`,
and the deviation `E = q P² − 1` with `q = n_R² + R²D² + n_z² = R⁸|B|²` (so `W = P (1 + E)^{−1/2}`
is `q^{−1/2}` exactly). Generated by `scripts/gc_kam/gen_gcflow.py` (untrusted); every identity
below is checked by `ring` after pointwise evaluation.

**Identities** (for every point `x` of the strip algebra): `∂_u D = D_u` etc. (`pd_*`,
`phiD_*`), the symmetry of second partial derivatives (`sym_*`), the curl-free identities of `B`
(`curl1`, `curl2`, `curl3`), the relation `E = qP² − 1` and its derivatives (`E_val`, `E_d0`,
`E_d1`, `E_dph`), and `∂_z P = ∂_φ P = 0`.

**Sanity.** `PuP_zero`: `P(0) = 1`; `EpP_axis`: `E` vanishes on the magnetic axis `u = z = 0`.
-/

@[expose] public section
noncomputable section

namespace PlasmaLean.Design.RationalStellaratorGC

